Copy the generated https forwarding URL (e.g., https://abc123.ngrok.io) – this will be used as your Alexa endpoint.

7. ⚙️ Configure Alexa Developer Console
Go to Alexa Developer Console

Create a new skill (or open your existing one)

Under Endpoint, select:

HTTPS

Skill endpoint: paste the Ngrok URL + /alexa
Example: https://abc123.ngrok.io/alexa

Enable Account Linking (if required) and Skill ID verification

8. 🧪 Test the Skill
Use the Alexa Simulator in the developer console, or test with a real device linked to your account.

Try commands like:

“Alexa, open Bus Tracker”

“Alexa, set my location to 41.88 North and 87.63 West”

“Alexa, how far is bus 22 going north?”

9. 🧼 Stopping the Server
Stop Flask: CTRL+C

Stop Ngrok: CTRL+C

You’ll need to restart Ngrok each time (since the URL changes unless you have a paid account with reserved domains).

🔁 Optional: Persistent Hosting
To make this skill production-ready, consider deploying it to:

AWS Lambda via AWS API Gateway

EC2 or Elastic Beanstalk

Render, Heroku, or Railway (if Flask-compatible)

📘 Notes
Your Alexa skill must be in Development mode unless you submit it for public certification.

Alexa verifies the Skill ID – ensure it matches what’s in SkillAdapter() in your code.
